{"id":"mahabharata-6-022","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":22,"title":"द्वाविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 22 · The Pandava array and the first sounds of war","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira orders the army into formation against Bhishma, and the Pandava divisions move out under their leaders. The din of drums, conches and elephants rises from both armies.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ವ್ಯೂಹ ರಚಿಸುವಂತೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಆಜ್ಞಾಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವ ವಿಭಾಗಗಳು ನಾಯಕರ ನೇತೃತ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ಮುನ್ನಡೆಯುತ್ತವೆ. ಎರಡೂ ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳಿಂದ ಭೇರಿ, ಶಂಖ, ಆನೆಗಳ ಘೋಷ ಏಳುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर भीष्म के विरुद्ध सेना का व्यूह बनाने का आदेश देते हैं, और पाण्डव टुकड़ियाँ अपने नायकों के नेतृत्व में आगे बढ़ती हैं। दोनों सेनाओं से नगाड़ों, शंखों और हाथियों का शोर उठता है।","te":"భీష్మునికి ఎదురుగా వ్యూహం పన్నమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఆజ్ఞాపిస్తాడు; పాండవ దళాలు నాయకుల ఆధ్వర్యంలో ముందుకు సాగుతాయి. ఇరు సేనల నుండి భేరీలు, శంఖాలు, ఏనుగుల ధ్వని లేస్తుంది.","ta":"பீஷ்மருக்கு எதிராக அணிவகுக்க யுதிஷ்டிரர் ஆணையிட, பாண்டவப் பிரிவுகள் தலைவர்கள் வழிநடத்த முன்னேறுகின்றன. இரு படைகளிலிருந்தும் முரசு, சங்கு, யானைகளின் முழக்கம் எழுகிறது.","ml":"ഭീഷ്മരെ നേരിടാൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ സേനയെ അണിനിരത്തുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവ സൈന്യവിഭാഗങ്ങൾ അവരുടെ നേതാക്കളുടെ കീഴിൽ നീങ്ങുന്നു. ഇരുപക്ഷത്തുനിന്നും ഭേരികളുടെയും ശംഖുകളുടെയും ആനകളുടെയും ആരവം ഉയരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.22; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्गीतापर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadgita Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा स्वां सेनां समचोदयत् ।\nप्रतिव्यूहन्ननीकानि भीष्मस्य भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira urged on his own army, arraying his divisions against Bhishma's, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":2,"text":"यथोद्दिष्टान्यनीकानि प्रत्यव्यूहन्त पाण्डवाः ।\nस्वर्गं परमभीप्सन्तः सुयुद्धेन कुरूद्वहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, bulls of the Kurus, desiring the highest heaven by good fighting, arrayed their divisions as they had been set out."}},{"n":3,"text":"मध्ये शिखण्डिनोऽनीकं रक्षितं सव्यसाचिना ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नस्य च स्वयं भीमेन परिपालितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle was Shikhandin's division, guarded by Savyasachi, and Dhrishtadyumna's, personally protected by Bhima."}},{"n":4,"text":"अनीकं दक्षिणं राजन्युयुधानेन पालितम् ।\nश्रीमता सात्वताग्र्येण शक्रेणेव धनुष्मता ॥","meaning":{"en":"The right division, king, was guarded by Yuyudhana, the glorious best of the Satvatas, like Shakra with his bow."}},{"n":5,"text":"महेन्द्रयानप्रतिमं रथं तु\nसोपस्करं हाटकरत्नचित्रम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरः काञ्चनभाण्डयोक्त्रं\nसमास्थितो नागकुलस्य मध्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira stood in a chariot like Mahendra's vehicle, fully equipped, decked with gold and gems, with golden fittings and traces, in the midst of a herd of elephants."}},{"n":6,"text":"समुच्छ्रितं दान्तशलाकमस्य\nसुपाण्डुरं छत्रमतीव भाति ।\nप्रदक्षिणं चैनमुपाचरन्ति\nमहर्षयः संस्तुतिभिर्नरेन्द्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Above him a very pale umbrella with ivory ribs rose high and shone greatly, and great sages attended the king by circling him to the right, with praises."}},{"n":7,"text":"पुरोहिताः शत्रुवधं वदन्तो\nमहर्षिवृद्धाः श्रुतवन्त एव ।\nजप्यैश्च मन्त्रैश्च तथौषधीभिः\nसमन्ततः स्वस्त्ययनं प्रचक्रुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The priests, elders among the great sages and learned, speaking of the slaying of the foe, performed rites for his welfare on every side, with muttered prayers, mantras and herbs."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः स वस्त्राणि तथैव गाश्च\nफलानि पुष्पाणि तथैव निष्कान् ।\nकुरूत्तमो ब्राह्मणसान्महात्मा\nकुर्वन्ययौ शक्र इवामरेभ्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that best of the Kurus, the great-souled one, advanced giving garments, cows, fruits, flowers and gold coins to Brahmins, as Shakra gives to the immortals."}},{"n":9,"text":"सहस्रसूर्यः शतकिङ्किणीकः\nपरार्ध्यजाम्बूनदहेमचित्रः ।\nरथोऽर्जुनस्याग्निरिवार्चिमाली\nविभ्राजते श्वेतहयः सुचक्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna's chariot shone like a thousand suns, with a hundred bells, painted with fine Jambunada gold, white-horsed, with good wheels, like a blazing fire."}},{"n":10,"text":"तमास्थितः केशवसंगृहीतं\nकपिध्वजं गाण्डिवबाणहस्तः ।\nधनुर्धरो यस्य समः पृथिव्यां\nन विद्यते नो भविता वा कदाचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounted in it, with Keshava as charioteer, Arjuna with the monkey banner, with Gandiva and arrows in hand, had no equal as a bowman on earth, now or ever."}},{"n":11,"text":"उद्वर्तयिष्यंस्तव पुत्रसेना-\nमतीव रौद्रं स बिभर्ति रूपम् ।\nअनायुधो यः सुभुजो भुजाभ्यां\nनराश्वनागान्युधि भस्म कुर्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Intent on uprooting your son's army, he bore an exceedingly dreadful form; though weaponless, that man with fine arms could turn men, horses and elephants to ashes in battle with his two arms."}},{"n":12,"text":"स भीमसेनः सहितो यमाभ्यां\nवृकोदरो वीररथस्य गोप्ता ।\nतं प्रेक्ष्य मत्तर्षभसिंहखेलं\nलोके महेन्द्रप्रतिमानकल्पम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, with the twins, Vrikodara, guarded the heroic chariot; seeing him, the sport of a lion among rutting bulls, equal in the world to Mahendra."}},{"n":13,"text":"समीक्ष्य सेनाग्रगतं दुरासदं\nप्रविव्यथुः पङ्कगता इवोष्ट्राः ।\nवृकोदरं वारणराजदर्पं\nयोधास्त्वदीया भयविग्नसत्त्वाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, hard to approach, standing at the head of the army with the pride of a king of elephants, your warriors, hearts shaken with fear, trembled like camels in mud."}},{"n":14,"text":"अनीकमध्ये तिष्ठन्तं राजपुत्रं दुरासदम् ।\nअब्रवीद्भरतश्रेष्ठं गुडाकेशं जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana spoke to Gudakesha, the best of the Bharatas and prince, who stood in the middle of the army, hard to approach."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"य एष गोप्ता प्रतपन्बलस्थो\nयो नः सेनां सिंह इवेक्षते च ।\nस एष भीष्मः कुरुवंशकेतु-\nर्येनाहृतास्त्रिंशतो वाजिमेधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This protector who stands burning in his strength and looks over our army like a lion, is Bhishma, the banner of the Kuru line, by whom thirty horse sacrifices were performed.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"एतान्यनीकानि महानुभावं\nगूहन्ति मेघा इव घर्मरश्मिम् ।\nएतानि हत्वा पुरुषप्रवीर\nकाङ्क्षस्व युद्धं भरतर्षभेण ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These divisions hide that mighty one as clouds hide the hot-rayed sun. Having killed them, best of men, seek battle with the bull of the Bharatas.\""}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"केषां प्रहृष्टास्तत्राग्रे योधा युध्यन्ति संजय ।\nउदग्रमनसः केऽत्र के वा दीना विचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, whose warriors fought gladly in front there, and who were high-spirited, who downcast and bewildered?"}},{"n":18,"text":"के पूर्वं प्राहरंस्तत्र युद्धे हृदयकम्पने ।\nमामकाः पाण्डवानां वा तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who struck first in that heart-shaking battle, my men or the Pandavas'? Tell me, Sanjaya."}},{"n":19,"text":"कस्य सेनासमुदये गन्धमाल्यसमुद्भवः ।\nवाचः प्रदक्षिणाश्चैव योधानामभिगर्जताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In whose army gathering arose the scent of perfumes and garlands, and who had warriors' shouts of auspicious right-hand sound?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"उभयोः सेनयोस्तत्र योधा जहृषिरे मुदा ।\nस्रग्धूपपानगन्धानामुभयत्र समुद्भवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The warriors in both armies rejoiced with delight, and in both, the scent of garlands, incense and drinks arose."}},{"n":21,"text":"संहतानामनीकानां व्यूढानां भरतर्षभ ।\nसंसर्पतामुदीर्णानां विमर्दः सुमहानभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, when the massed, arrayed armies advanced and surged, there was a very great crush."}},{"n":22,"text":"वादित्रशब्दस्तुमुलः शङ्खभेरीविमिश्रितः ।\nकुञ्जराणां च नदतां सैन्यानां च प्रहृष्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A tumultuous sound of musical instruments mixed with conchs and drums, of roaring elephants and of rejoicing troops."}}]}]}